      "description": "Watch Udinese vs Venezia highlights and goals from Coppa Italia on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 2, 2026. The tension of knockout football returned as Udinese and Venezia locked horns in a highly anticipated Coppa Italia fixture. Fans gathered on 2026-09-02 to witness which side would seize the initiative in this high-stakes cup encounter. Udinese Take Charge Early The match ignited almost immediately with Udinese showing clinical intent from the opening whistle. In the 9th minute, Richie Sagrado broke the deadlock with a well-taken goal, putting the hosts firmly in the driving seat. Venezia struggled to contain the early pressure, leading to a yellow card for Nicolo Bertola shortly after. The momentum stayed with the home side throughout the first half, and their persistence paid off again in the 34th minute when Vakoun Issouf Bayo found the net, courtesy of a precise assist from Mergim Vojvoda . Clinical Finishing and Tactical Control As the second half got underway, the home side showed no signs of slowing down despite a tactical change from the visitors that saw James Abankwah replace Bertola . In the 53rd minute, Vakoun Issouf Bayo struck again to secure his brace, finishing a move started by Keinan Davis . With a three-goal cushion, the match entered a phase of heavy rotations. Managers utilized their benches extensively, with Idrissa Gueye , Hassane Kamara , and Enzo Ebosse entering for Udinese , while Venezia introduced Akor Adams in hopes of a late resurgence. However, the hosts maintained their defensive discipline until the final whistle blew at 90+4 minutes."
